# Consumer root expression (caos design/flake-inputs.md, "Consumer root").
# Two steps, chained through a variable:
#   1. MOUNTED — splice caos's std/ into this tree at caos-std/. Nothing of
#      caos is committed; the loader checks the pin below against the `caos`
#      input in flake.lock and refuses a drifted one.
#   2. deepen the mounted tree, so each ./DEPS line becomes a DEEP-DEPS/<name>
#      mount. That second step is what `run-tool` needs: it resolves a tool
#      script's image as DEEP-DEPS/bash, which does not exist until the tree
#      is deepened. Without it every tool call fails to resolve its image.
MOUNTED=run --base:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d3407c55592e7e9454ad9413a8ac9d5a0e3b7c05&dir=std/flake-input-loader --input-tree:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d3407c55592e7e9454ad9413a8ac9d5a0e3b7c05&dir=std --input=caos --in:@=. --expr=$CAOS_EXPR --output-path=caos-std
run --base:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d3407c55592e7e9454ad9413a8ac9d5a0e3b7c05&dir=std/deep-deps --in=$MOUNTED
